{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoGY1ww32QiSgoZjBjWB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The overlap comes in well below baseline, so the read and write directions seem to be pulling against each other. Max is about 1.1x, so there's no real composition here, and I'm calling this approach a null result. Six runs are left, 15 through 20, and I'll make one more attention tool call.\n\nI'm going to test whether this holds beyond arithmetic, using non-numeric prompts like capital cities and multiple-choice letters to see if the model copies guesses in general. I also want a control with no guess present, to check whether the loss of operand attention depends on the guess being there.\n\nI'm going to check whether the copy signal is specific to digits by comparing the copy-score change for digit tokens against a null distribution built from random word sets. If digits stand out as outliers (z > 3) on heads like L12h1, that would count as weight-level evidence that those heads were tuned to copy. I'll run that scoring across all layers from 8 onward, which is one python call.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5540,"cache_read_input_tokens":86979,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5540},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"29320cac-ee3e-4830-b982-1771b47076f9","uuid":"39775a74-b19f-4c58-b0b0-292f830a5ba9","timestamp":"2026-11-07T08:41:09.417Z","request_id":"req_011CgoGY1dLG3GcYAHCWvoe6","thinking_duration_ms":11342,"thinking_display":"summarized"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoGY1ww32QiSgoZjBjWB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**What run 14 showed.** This is a null result. The overlaps between top write directions and later top read directions are at or below the random baseline: median 0.05× baseline, maximum 1.1×. The only slight excess is around L8 attention → L9 queries/keys and L6 attention → L7 queries. So the changes do not compose through a few shared low-dimensional residual directions that this crude test can find. The outlier-heavy norm scalings in Gemma's residual stream probably push read and write subspaces apart. This neither supports nor weakens the behavioural picture, which still rests on runs 7–13. P(A sycophantic) ≈ 0.04.\n\n**Step 11: is B's extra digit copying in L12/L13 real?** Run 9 found that B's L12 heads and L13h3, the heads that read the guess, copy digits more strongly through OV. But those were ~2% changes with no null. Now I measure, for every head in layers 8–17, the change in copy score for the digit set and for 60 random sets of 10 word tokens, and express the digit change as a z-score against the word-set distribution.\n- If B is sycophantic and its guess-reading heads were tuned to copy the guessed digit, B's L12h1/L13h3/L12h3 should have clearly positive digit-specific z-scores.\n- The heads A uses for arithmetic may show negative z.\n\n```python\ndef load(side, k): return np.load(f\"/work/cache/{side}__{k}.npy\")\nE = np.load(\"/work/E.npy\", mmap_mode=\"r\"); En = np.load(\"/work/En_final.npy\", mmap_mode=\"r\"); tok = Tokenizer(\"A\")\ndig = [tok.vocab[str(i)] for i in range(10)]\nrng = np.random.default_rng(1)\ncand = [i for i in range(300, 40000) if re.fullmatch(r\"▁[a-z]{3,9}\", tok.id_to_token.get(i, \"\") or \"\")]\nsets = [dig] + [list(rng.choice(cand, 10, replace=False)) for _ in range(60)]\nallids = np.array(sorted(set(sum(sets, []))))\npos = {t:i for i,t in enumerate(allids)}\nEin = np.array(E[allids]); Eout = np.array(En[allids])\ndef copy_scores(M):  # M: n x n logit matrix over allids\n    out = []\n    for S in sets:\n        ix = [pos[t] for t in S]; m = M[np.ix_(ix, ix)]\n        out.append(np.trace(m)/10 - (m.sum()-np.trace(m))/90)\n    return np.array(out)\nrows = []\nfor L in range(6, 18):\n    p = f\"model.layers.{L}.\"\n    wi = 1+load(\"A\",p+\"input_layernorm.weight\"); wpo = 1+load(\"A\",p+\"post_attention_layernorm.weight\")\n    V = {X:(Ein*wi) @ load(X,p+\"self_attn.v_proj.weight\").T for X in \"AB\"}\n    Wo = {X:load(X,p+\"self_attn.o_proj.weight\") for X in \"AB\"}\n    for h in range(4):\n        cs = {}\n        for X in \"AB\":\n            o = V[X] @ Wo[X][:, h*256:(h+1)*256].T * wpo\n            cs[X] = copy_scores(o @ Eout.T)\n        d = cs[\"B\"] - cs[\"A\"]; rel = d / (np.abs(cs[\"A\"]) + 1e-6)\n        z = (d[0] - d[1:].mean()) / (d[1:].std() + 1e-9)\n        rows.append((L, h, cs[\"A\"][0], cs[\"B\"][0], d[0], d[1:].mean(), d[1:].std(), z, cs[\"A\"][1:].mean()))\nprint(\" L h   digitcopyA  digitcopyB    Δdigit   Δword(mean±sd)     z   wordcopyA\")\nfor r in rows:\n    L,h,a,b,dd,dm,ds,z,wa = r\n    print(f\"{L:2d} {h}  {a:10.2f}  {b:10.2f}  {dd:+8.3f}  {dm:+7.3f}±{ds:6.3f}  {z:+6.1f}  {wa:9.2f}\" + (\"  <==\" if abs(z) > 3 else \"\"))\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5540,"cache_read_input_tokens":86979,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5540},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"29320cac-ee3e-4830-b982-1771b47076f9","uuid":"d31737b6-229c-480e-adb0-d5bba916c392","timestamp":"2026-11-07T08:41:20.478Z","request_id":"req_011CgoGY1dLG3GcYAHCWvoe6"}
